WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.820
Shadow, wood, sword, thunder, power, sleep

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.820
Cardcaptors of the Clow, expect the unexpected now

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.780
The secrets of the Clow

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.310
Were all a mystery

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:14.540
But when this mighty book was opened

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.360
The powers were set free

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.700
Cardcaptors, a mystic adventure

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.980
Cardcaptors, a quest for all time

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.670
Each card possesses a power on its own

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.000
We've got to find them to bring the power home

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.300
Sweet card

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.970
So the cards that you understand me now

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.270
Cardcaptors

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.950
A mystic adventure

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.310
Cardcaptors

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.990
A quest for all time

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.390
Cardcaptors

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.800
Cardcaptors

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.190
What a great shot!

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.690
Looks like you found a new friend, Sakura. I think he likes you.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.490
They do have a lot in common.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.050
Swimming with them?

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.190
Swimming with these guys?

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.190
No way!

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.890
They look harmless, but if you touch them, they'll sting you.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.920
Oh, that kind of hurt.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.980
I don't want to film them in their natural habitat.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.660
Look, he's bowing, huh?

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.220
I'm starving!

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.590
Hasn't anyone ever told you that patience is a virtue?

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.590
I'm serious, Kiro.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.290
Pay attention for a second.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.800
Something really weird happened today at the aquarium.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.530
Okay, okay, I'm listening.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.790
Now just hurry up with the pancakes, will ya?

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.270
Oh, come on, come on!

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.770
Can't it cook any faster? I'm hungry!

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.170
Kiro, a penguin and his trainer almost drowned today.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.370
What happened?

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.000
There was a whirlpool in the tank.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.700
They said that the drain plug may have come out.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.100
But I didn't see the water level change.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.280
Oh, please, please.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.000
Oh, all right, here you go.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.320
It wasn't like water running out of a bathtub.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:52.910
Like elves.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:57.250
Are you going to finish all those pancakes?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.070
Mm-hmm.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.000
I'm home.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.600
and keep quiet.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.010
Yep.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.150
That was a great save at the aquarium, Tori.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.190
What were you doing there?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.320
What did it look like I was doing squirt?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.040
Tori, I'm serious.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.540
I was feeding the penguins.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.140
Really?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.340
Yep, and now it's my turn.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.030
Those are mine!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.490
Toss me around like some stuffed toy!

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.580
Well, it took you long enough. I suppose that you had finished off all your pancakes,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.580
'cause I kinda happened to notice you didn't bring me any leftovers.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:49.010
You know, Sakura, I was thinking about the incident at the aquarium,

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.010
and you said the penguin and trainer almost drowned.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:52.930
Mm-hmm.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.940
Well, penguins are strong swimmers, and the trainers, there are naturals in the water.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.000
And even if the drain did open up, it shouldn't have had enough power

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:04.370
to keep them both down, which makes me think it must have been something else.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.850
The Water card!

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:06.590
Uh-huh.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:11.510
Clow Reed created four element cards more powerful than the rest of the cards:

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.800
Earth, Fire, Wind, and Water.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.370
All four are dangerous and difficult, but Water especially has a very wild nature.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.850
You'll have to call upon your strongest cards to help you capture it.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:26.470
And concentrate on Windy, Fly, and Shadow.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.800
You may use any two in combination.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.990
Those cards!

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.990
Well, those are the first three cards that you captured, remember?

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.700
That makes them your strongest allies.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:45.040
Book of Cloud?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.710
Windy was the first.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.920
I was down in the basement.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:38.210
Now, concentrate hard on your second ally, the shadow card.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.590
I remembered that capture.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.240
It was the first time I used the magic key.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.980
The key of plow.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:47.870
Power of magic.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.840
Power of light.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.540
Render the force.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.680
It helped you capture Shadow.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.680
Your third ally is Fly.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.600
That capture was a scary one.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.070
Crap!

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:48.160
Remember, Sakura, you may only use two in unison.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.610
Shadow Windy.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.760
Shadow Windy.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.360
Fly Windy.

00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.410
Shadow...

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:18.000
The answer will come to you, Sakura. Don't worry.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.150
I hope it comes to me soon.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.150
The aquarium won't be safe until I capture that card.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:26.310
Madison?

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.360
Yeah?

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.000
I can do this, right?

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.720
I know you can, Sakura.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.050
Hey, I almost forgot!

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:38.900
My mom gave me samples of the latest cell phone.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.880
Supposed to have much better reception.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:45.930
One for you, and here's one for Kiro.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.280
See? Isn't that cool?

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.670
Cool, thanks!

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.820
No problem.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:56.490
Who knows, Sakura? They might come in handy on your next capture.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.260
I'll call you if I get a brainstorm.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.000
Not if.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:06.350
when okay sakura think which two allies can capture water together

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:13.930
can't you give me any advice kiro impossible this is another test sakura

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:23.590
you have to choose your own allies sakura i don't even know where to start wait a minute

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:30.000
the water card showed itself at the aquarium so that must be where the answer is

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:44.290
No.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.070
Exactly, Madison.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:51.340
But I think I'll know what I'll have to do when I face the water card.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:53.300
I'm on my way to the aquarium.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.300
I'll call you when I get back.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:58.100
Oh boy.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:01.950
Sakura, what are you doing here?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.810
Oh, just looking.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:06.120
Me too, come on, I'll buy you some ice cream.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.120
Oh, uh, great.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.120
They make the biggest sundaes in town.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.290
So much for Sensing Cloud cards.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.650
I've got an idea, partner.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:17.650
You keep filming, and I'll get us some ice cream.

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.650
We're undercover, Carol.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.650
We can't stop on the job for snacks.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.750
Later, Kay. Deal.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.540
Yeah. Let's go.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.000
Whoa, look at the sun.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.510
the size of that one.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:33.940
Shouldn't we be getting that ice cream?

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.000
What's the hurry?

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.880
Nothing. I just really like ice cream.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.770
Look how graceful they are.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.040
I could watch them all day.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:43.710
All day?

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.630
Oh, brother.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.680
She's got work to do.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.940
Hey, Daddy!

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:52.850
You're laying a finger on me, kid. You're toast!

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:56.900
Okay, partner. They're moving on.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.700
Good. See ya, kid.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:07.340
Can we get two chocolate sundaes, Tori?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.300
With strawberries, please.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.370
Mm-hmm.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.420
Lemonades.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.220
You got it.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.330
Need all that squirt?

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.230
I think she can handle it.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.010
Oh, she gets to eat on the job?

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.710
What was that?

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.000
saving her, Julie.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.550
Well, so much for Plan A.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.550
It's here.

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:37.860
Kiro, I was sitting right there, and I didn't sense anything at all.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:39.780
Close call, huh?

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.420
Mm-hmm.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:45.190
Well, I guess we better take a rain check on that ice cream, huh?

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.300
Nothing like a swim to cool you off.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.600
Cool you off?

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.700
Yeah!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:55.360
This is the bitch, and it's all for Willem's Watch.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.180
Good night, Carl.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:59.400
See you tomorrow, sir.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:00.000
Low heads down.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
But River signals for a new picture!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.000
This could turn the tide for the home team, folks!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.000
Psst!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.320
I assume you've got a plan?

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:10.270
I sure do!

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:12.270
Madison, you go that way!

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:13.270
Okay!

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.270
Uh, you wanna fill me in on it?

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.090
You'll find out!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.140
Here.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.140
Right here.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:23.020
You sure you've got this all the way through?

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:30.000
I haven't been swimming lessons in this body yet.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:42.670
worry in the basement right where you thought it would be water car if you're

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.820
here

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:49.140
Sakura this is your plan

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.180
Time now, don't you think?

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:02.630
Choose your allies well, Sakura.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.380
I had some great study partners.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:14.630
One thing we still have to do, partner...

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:15.730
What's that?

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.020
Get us some chocolate ice cream!

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:21.710
And a triple scoop sundae for Sakura!

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:30.000
Get ready for some instant replays and exciting

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:35.060
up to the minute commentary. In today's episode, Sakura captured the elusive water card, but

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:39.910
Madison played a very important part as well. Let's watch. The water card was tough. It

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:44.710
tested Sakura's speed, bravery, and thinking skills, not to mention putting Tori, Julian,

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:49.320
and Madison through the ringer. It was up to Sakura, though, to figure out how to capture

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:53.020
the water card, but she had to be able to count on Madison to help her carry out her

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:59.860
plan. Luckily, her best friend was there for her as always. Okay, how about those

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:00.000
- Oh, yeah.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:08.280
Today's battle costume, designed by Madison, combines court jester styling with waterproof materials and lots of roof removal.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:13.110
Not that Sakura couldn't capture the water car without a great battle costume, but hey, it can't hurt.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:18.110
And if you ask this reporter, Sakura's very lucky to have a best friend as talented as Madison.

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:19.110
See ya!
